<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Refer to the file <a href="https://github.com/google-parfait/federated-compute/blob/main/fcp/protos/confidentialcompute/access_policy.proto" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href ltx_font_typewriter">access_policy.proto</a> in the GitHub repository <a href="https://github.com/google-parfait/federated-compute" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">google-parfait/federated-compute</a> for more exposition on the policy structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Autotuning</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Why Autotuning Requires DP Quantiles</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that we replaced the DP quantile algorithm in our autotuning system with a deterministic algorithm. We will demonstrate that such a variant is vulnerable to an attack that deduces which group a privacy unit contributes to, even when the tuned parameters are hidden from the attacker.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the case where (a) the user’s query requests a summation of one value, with <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">L_inf<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1</annotation></semantics></math></span> but <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_groups_contributed</span> is not specified (b) Alice contributes to either the group “normal” or both groups “normal” and “embarrassing.” Because of (a), our system marks <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_groups_contributed</span> as the sole parameter to tune. This means it will add noise proportional to the <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=83" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>83</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=83</annotation></semantics></math>rd percentile of the number of groups that a privacy unit contributes to. If the adversary mixes Alice’s (encrypted) input with 82 copies of “normal” privacy units and 17 copies of units that contribute to both “normal” and “embarrassing” then (b) implies that the number of groups Alice contributes to will be the 83rd percentile, which directly reveals which of the two inputs she has.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If the adversary directly observes the 83rd percentile, they can deduce whether she has contributed to “embarrassing” simply by mapping 2 to “yes” and 1 to “no.” If they do not, recall that the noise added to the sums is scaled proportional to the choice of <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_groups_contributed</span>; because the attacker has control over the Alice’s peers, they can measure the noise via subtraction of pre-noise values and apply a likelihood test to determine which of the two distributions it was sampled from.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, our analysis will make the assumption that we are tuning one parameter; to generalize to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> parameters, we can divide failure probabilities by <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the union bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> positive scalar values over which we are computing the <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile; if we are tuning <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">L_inf</span> for example then the <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th scalar is the maximum contribution to any group that the <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th privacy unit makes. Our autotuning process proceeds as follows:</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each element of <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, toss a coin with head-bias <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\ll 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\ll 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> scalars whose coin landed heads; note that <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\sim\mathbf{Bin}(n,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁𝐢𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\sim\mathbf{Bin}(n,q)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Feed <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> into our <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-DP quantile algorithm to estimate the <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Report the outcome of that algorithm as an estimate of the <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For any multiset <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we will say that we have a “<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>” when its index in (sorted) <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> lies inside the interval <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\gamma}(T):=[\frac{k-\gamma}{100}\cdot|T|,\penalty\ \frac{k+\gamma}{100}\cdot|T|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\gamma}(T):=[\frac{k-\gamma}{100}\cdot|T|,\penalty\ \frac{k+\gamma}{100}\cdot|T|]</annotation></semantics></math>, the indices of values within <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>% of the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile. <em id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Our driving question is to find a setting of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that the outcome 10-approximates the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that there are two sources of error: the sampling of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and the DP algorithm. This appendix has one section for each. First, we find the range of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> 5-approximates the <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, except with probability <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we find the range of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that the DP algorithm will report a 5-approximation of the <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, except with probability <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Putting these two parts together with <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1/30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1/30</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that we have a range of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that the outcome 10-approximates the <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, 90% of the time.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.1 </span>Sampling rate to ensure representativeness</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of elements in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> that are less than the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-5)</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of elements in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> that lie between the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-5)</annotation></semantics></math>-th and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+5)</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentiles of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of elements in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> that are greater than the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+5)</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">If we could show <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&lt;\frac{k}{100}|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&lt;\frac{k}{100}|S|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;\frac{100-k}{100}|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;\frac{100-k}{100}|S|</annotation></semantics></math>, then the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> approximates the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>: the first inequality implies that the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is larger than the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-5)</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and the second implies it is smaller than the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+5)</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=a+b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=a+b+c</annotation></semantics></math>, we can rewrite our desired constraints:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a&lt;{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a&lt;{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}|S|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}(a+b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}(a+b+c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}a&lt;{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}a&lt;{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}(b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}(b+c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{k}a&lt;{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{k}a&lt;{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b+c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c&lt;{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c&lt;{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}|S|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}(a+b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}(a+b+c)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}c&lt;{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100}c&lt;{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}(a+b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{100}(a+b)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100-k}c&lt;{}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100-k}c&lt;{}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a+b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">marginal</em> distributions are <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\sim\mathbf{Bin}(\frac{k-5}{100}n,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁𝐢𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sim\mathbf{Bin}(\frac{k-5}{100}n,q)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\sim\mathbf{Bin}(\frac{1}{10}n,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁𝐢𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\sim\mathbf{Bin}(\frac{1}{10}n,q)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\sim\mathbf{Bin}(\frac{95-k}{100}n,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁𝐢𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\sim\mathbf{Bin}(\frac{95-k}{100}n,q)</annotation></semantics></math>. We will use a concentration inequality and a union bound to derive constraints on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that we can derive (<a href="#A2.Ex4" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.Ex8" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is a binomial with mean <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the multiplicative Chernoff bound<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
              It is also possible to use the additive Hoeffding bound, but recall we target <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\ll 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\ll 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> in which case the multiplicative bound is tighter.</span></span></span> implies the two inequalities below:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[|\eta-\mu|\geq\psi\mu\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[|\eta-\mu|\geq\psi\mu\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\exp(-\psi^{2}\mu/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\exp(-\psi^{2}\mu/3)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[\eta\leq(1-\psi)\mu\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[\eta\leq(1-\psi)\mu\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp(-\psi^{2}\mu/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp(-\psi^{2}\mu/2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We apply these tail bounds to the marginals of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[\left|a-\frac{k-5}{100}nq\right|\geq\psi\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}nq\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[\left|a-\frac{k-5}{100}nq\right|\geq\psi\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}nq\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ \penalty\ \leq 2\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\left({\frac{k-5}{100}nq}\right)/3}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ \penalty\ \leq 2\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\left({\frac{k-5}{100}nq}\right)/3}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[b\leq(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{1}{10}nq\right]}\leq\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\left({\frac{1}{10}nq}\right)/2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[b\leq(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{1}{10}nq\right]}\leq\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\left({\frac{1}{10}nq}\right)/2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[\left|c-\frac{95-k}{100}nq\right|\geq\psi\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}nq\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}\left[\left|c-\frac{95-k}{100}nq\right|\geq\psi\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}nq\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ \penalty\ \leq 2\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\left({\frac{95-k}{100}nq}\right)/3}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \penalty\ \penalty\ \leq 2\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\left({\frac{95-k}{100}nq}\right)/3}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">A union bound implies that we can safely assume all three of the inequalities</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|a-\frac{k-5}{100}nq\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|a-\frac{k-5}{100}nq\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\psi\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\psi\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{1}{10}nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{1}{10}nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|c-\frac{95-k}{100}nq\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|c-\frac{95-k}{100}nq\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\psi\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\psi\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">are simultaneously true, except with probability</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\leq 5\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\cdot\min\left({\frac{k-5}{300},\frac{1}{20},\frac{95-k}{300}}\right)\cdot nq}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 5\exp\left({-\psi^{2}\cdot\min\left({\frac{k-5}{300},\frac{1}{20},\frac{95-k}{300}}\right)\cdot nq}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p">So to target a failure probability of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, we should ensure</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{q\geq\frac{1}{\psi^{2}n}\cdot\max\left({\frac{300}{k-5},20,\frac{300}{95-k}}\right)\cdot\ln\frac{5}{\beta}.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{q\geq\frac{1}{\psi^{2}n}\cdot\max\left({\frac{300}{k-5},20,\frac{300}{95-k}}\right)\cdot\ln\frac{5}{\beta}.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.5" class="ltx_p">Once we upper bound <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, we will have our desired result. We do so by combining (<a href="#A2.Ex4" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.Ex8" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) with the concentration bounds. To ensure (<a href="#A2.Ex4" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), it will suffice to show that an upper bound on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100-k}{k}a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100-k}{k}a</annotation></semantics></math> is less than a lower bound on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{k}a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{k}a</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{100-k}{k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{100-k}{k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b+c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\frac{105-k}{100}\cdot(1-\psi)\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>105</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\frac{105-k}{100}\cdot(1-\psi)\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.6" class="ltx_p">So it suffices for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100-k}{k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}\cdot nq&lt;\frac{105-k}{100}\cdot(1-\psi)\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>105</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100-k}{k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}\cdot nq&lt;\frac{105-k}{100}\cdot(1-\psi)\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math> to imply (<a href="#A2.Ex4" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{100-k}{k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{k-5}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{105-k}{100}\cdot(1-\psi)\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>105</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{105-k}{100}\cdot(1-\psi)\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1+\psi}{1-\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1+\psi}{1-\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{k(105-k)}{(k-5)(100-k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>105</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{k(105-k)}{(k-5)(100-k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure (<a href="#A2.Ex8" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), it will suffice to show that an upper bound on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{k}{100-k}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{k}{100-k}c</annotation></semantics></math> is less than a lower bound on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100-k}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100-k}c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{k}{100-k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{k}{100-k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a+b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{k+5}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{k+5}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">So it suffices for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{k}{100-k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}\cdot nq&lt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{k+5}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{k}{100-k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}\cdot nq&lt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{k+5}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math> to imply (<a href="#A2.Ex8" title="In B.2.1 Sampling rate to ensure representativeness ‣ B.2 Mathematical Analysis of Autotuning ‣ Appendix B Autotuning ‣ Toward provably private analytics and insights into GenAI use" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{100-k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{100-k}\cdot(1+\psi)\cdot\frac{95-k}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{k+5}{100}\cdot nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;(1-\psi)\cdot\frac{k+5}{100}\cdot nq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1+\psi}{1-\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1+\psi}{1-\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{(100-k)(k+5)}{k(95-k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{(100-k)(k+5)}{k(95-k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, we should set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1+\psi}{1-\psi}&lt;\underbrace{\min\left({\frac{k(105-k)}{(k-5)(100-k)},\frac{(100-k)(k+5)}{k(95-k)}}\right)}_{z}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>105</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>z</mi></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1+\psi}{1-\psi}&lt;\underbrace{\min\left({\frac{k(105-k)}{(k-5)(100-k)},\frac{(100-k)(k+5)}{k(95-k)}}\right)}_{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">This simplifies to the inequality <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\psi&lt;\frac{z-1}{z+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\psi&lt;\frac{z-1}{z+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>; in practice, we search for this value numerically</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.2 </span>Sampling rate to ensure accurate DP quantile estimation</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first find an integer <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> such that when the sample size <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, our DP algorithm will 5-approximate the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th percentile of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> except with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we find a range of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> except with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Size of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure accurate DP quantile estimation</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with a brief sketch of the quantile-finding algorithm. It implements a simple variant of the <span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AboveThreshold</span> algorithm. The first idea is to divide the non-negative reals into a grid, where the grid points first follow linear growth then transition to exponential growth. At each point on this grid, the algorithm makes a noisy measurement of the number of inputs that are to the left. The output is the first grid point where this measurement exceeds a noisy threshold.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A bit more precisely,</p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initialize <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leftarrow 0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leftarrow 0.1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∼</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\sim</annotation></semantics></math> a Laplace distribution with scale <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> has not crossed the maximum representable value,</p>
<ol id="A2.I2.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{p}\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{p}\sim</annotation></semantics></math> a Laplace distribution with scale <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{S}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{S}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of inputs that are at most <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{S}(p)+\eta_{p}\geq\frac{k}{100}\cdot m+\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{S}(p)+\eta_{p}\geq\frac{k}{100}\cdot m+\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, break</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Else, <math id="A2.I2.i3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leftarrow\max(p+0.1,p\cdot 1.01)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1.01</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leftarrow\max(p+0.1,p\cdot 1.01)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Return <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Refer to the <span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DPQuantileAggregator</span> class in our library for the complete code.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming the maximum is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{64}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>64</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{64}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of Laplace random variables is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1+10+64\log_{1.01}2&lt;4470" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>1.01</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4470</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1+10+64\log_{1.01}2&lt;4470</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Except with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, all Laplace random variables have magnitude <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4470</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\frac{4}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means the algorithm will never halt on some <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{k}{100}\cdot m-f_{S}(p)&gt;\frac{8}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4470</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{k}{100}\cdot m-f_{S}(p)&gt;\frac{8}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the same logic, it will never continue once it has found some <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{S}(p)-\frac{k}{100}\cdot m&gt;\frac{8}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4470</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{S}(p)-\frac{k}{100}\cdot m&gt;\frac{8}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The upshot is that when <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{m\geq m^{*}:=\frac{160}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>160</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4470</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{m\geq m^{*}:=\frac{160}{\varepsilon}\ln\frac{4470}{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> bounds the probability that the returned <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is not an approximation of a value inside of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{5}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{5}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. The error of approximation is either an additive <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> or a relative <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampling rate to ensure minimum size of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we choose <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> such that the random variable <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|</annotation></semantics></math> is above the requisite threshold <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> except with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If we want <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq m^{*}\right]}\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq m^{*}\right]}\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and the multiplicative Chernoff bound implies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq(1-\psi)nq\right]}\leq\exp(-\psi^{2}nq/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq(1-\psi)nq\right]}\leq\exp(-\psi^{2}nq/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, it will suffice to show</p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq m^{*}\right]}\leq{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq(1-\psi)nq\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq m^{*}\right]}\leq{\mathbb{P}\left[|S|\leq(1-\psi)nq\right]}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\exp(-\psi^{2}nq/2)\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(-\psi^{2}nq/2)\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The constraint (a) is equivalent to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}\leq(1-\psi)nq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}\leq(1-\psi)nq</annotation></semantics></math> which is the same as <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq\frac{m^{*}}{(1-\psi)n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq\frac{m^{*}}{(1-\psi)n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Meanwhile, constraint (b) is equivalent to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 2\ln(1/\beta)/n\psi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 2\ln(1/\beta)/n\psi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, it suffices for</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{q\geq\max\left({\frac{2}{n\psi^{2}}\ln\frac{1}{\beta},\frac{m^{*}}{(1-\psi)n}}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{q\geq\max\left({\frac{2}{n\psi^{2}}\ln\frac{1}{\beta},\frac{m^{*}}{(1-\psi)n}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to find <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the above. The first function is a decreasing function of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> while the former is an increasing function, which means the minimum of the maximum is achieved where they intersect. In turn, we just need to <span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">solve the quadratic</span> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\psi^{2}=(1-\psi)\frac{2}{m^{*}}\ln(1/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\psi^{2}=(1-\psi)\frac{2}{m^{*}}\ln(1/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>; in practice, we search for this value numerically.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
